---


        
          
            
# Porting Reference

    

Complete guide for porting OpenBMC to a new platform.


  Creating the Machine Layer    
1. [Layer Structure](#layer-structure)
2. [layer.conf](#layerconf)
3. [machine.conf](#machineconf)

  
  Device Tree Configuration    
1. [Example Device Tree](#example-device-tree)

  
  GPIO Configuration    
1. [GPIO Pin Mapping](#gpio-pin-mapping)
2. [Power Control Configuration](#power-control-configuration)

  
  Entity Manager Configuration    
1. [Board Configuration](#board-configuration)
2. [Recipe for Configuration](#recipe-for-configuration)

  
  Verification Testing    
1. [Boot Test](#boot-test)
2. [Sensor Test](#sensor-test)
3. [Power Control Test](#power-control-test)
4. [Network Test](#network-test)

  
  Common Pitfalls    
1. [Device Tree Issues](#device-tree-issues)
2. [I2C Issues](#i2c-issues)
3. [Service Failures](#service-failures)

  
  Debugging During Porting    
1. [Early Boot Debugging](#early-boot-debugging)
2. [Kernel Debug Configuration](#kernel-debug-configuration)
3. [Memory and Runtime Debugging](#memory-and-runtime-debugging)

  
  eSPI Configuration
  References

---

## Overview

    

Porting OpenBMC to a new platform involves creating a machine layer, configuring hardware-specific components, and integrating with the build system.

**ARM Server Platforms**: For ARM-based servers (NVIDIA Grace, Ampere, etc.), see the [ARM Platform Guide](/openbmc-guide-tutorial/docs/06-porting/06-arm-platform-guide.html) which covers ARM-specific boot flow, meta-arm integration, and NVIDIA OpenBMC as a reference.

```mermaid
---
title: Porting Architecture
---
flowchart TB
    subgraph yourlayer["Your Machine Layer (meta-myplatform)"]
        direction LR
        machineconf["conf/machine/  
myboard.conf"]
        recipes["recipes-*  
(customization)"]
        layerconf["conf/layer.conf  
(layer metadata)"]
    end

    subgraph baselayers["OpenBMC Base Layers"]
        direction LR
        phosphor["meta-phosphor  
(services)"]
        aspeed["meta-aspeed  
(BMC SoC)"]
        oe["meta-openembedded  
(base packages)"]
    end

    subgraph buildsys["BitBake Build System"]
        bitbake["openbmc-env, bitbake"]
    end

    yourlayer --> baselayers
    baselayers --> buildsys
```

> **ASCII-art version (for comparison)**

  
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Porting Architecture                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                 │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐│
